  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "The third exit on a highway is located at milepost \\(40\\) and the tenth exit is at milepost \\(160.\\) There is a service center on the highway located three-fourths of the way from the third exit to the tenth exit. At what milepost would you expect to find this service center?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(90\\)",
    "B": "\\(100\\)",
    "C": "\\(110\\)",
    "D": "\\(120\\)",
    "E": "\\(130\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The fraction describes the distance between the two exits, so first find that distance:\n\\[\n160-40=120\\text{ miles}.\n\\]\nThree-fourths of this distance is\n\\[\n\\frac34\\cdot120=90\\text{ miles}.\n\\]\nStarting at milepost \\(40\\) and traveling \\(90\\) miles toward milepost \\(160\\) puts the service center at \\(40+90=130\\). The answer is milepost \\(130\\), choice \\(\\text{E}\\).",
